far cry 6 is a game about revolution  home brew weapons  pet alligators hobbled together  tentacles and  super moves yeah far cry 6 is very much  a far cry game and it seems to be  leaning even more heavily into the  series dangerous but  tongue-in-cheek mechanics in this video  we're going to go over  everything we've learned so far from  ubisoft about this game e3  2021 is right around the corner and  gamespot will have a ton to show during  our play for all events so make sure to  give us a thumbs up and subscribe to the  channel  so you don't miss out let's get to it  one thing hammered home in our preview  of far cry 6 was that the loadout of  your character will matter  and picking the right tools is important  weapons are highly customizable and gear  comes with specialized perks  loadouts can accommodate a number of  playstyles meaning that you can now  holster your weapon and try not to draw  attention you can sneak around  you can pay bribes to different enemies  hijack trucks and commit sabotage you  could also just play it like a standard  shooter  there are 49 weapons with plenty of  attachments and while we didn't see any  kind of stat space weapon rarity like in  far cry new dawn  we did see a range of categories when it  comes to arms juan cortes is your weapon  supplier  on the island of er he's basically cue  from james  the two bond together like fire and fury  through him or in the world you can get  different weapons across the regular  resolver and supremos category regular  weapons seem to be leftover guns from  last century's cold war like the sks  fal and m16 but also there's everyday  items like baseball bats throwing knives  make their return as a stealth go-to  weapon  next door resolve their weapons which  are hand-built improvised items  these range from mildly plausible like  the flamethrower  silent nail gun and emp grenades to the  ludicrous  like a minigun built from motorcycle  parts and a vinyl record launcher that  plays macarena  you've seen this stuff in far cry before  but this game is taking that over the  top and improvised aspect  a bit further there are also some very  silly improvised mechanics like  healing through pressing a lit cigar to  your wound above resolve air weapons we  have the sopremos that means far cry now  has super moves in the form of an  upgradeable backpack we are now headed  into  just cause territory  some of the supremos demonstrated in our  preview was a backpack mortar launcher  that could clear an area and also a  rocket jump this all ties into far cry  6's rpg  light gear system which includes perks  clothing can do things like improve your  headshot damage  increase stealth and mobility or  guarantee throwing knives hit their  target we're not sure yet if that means  enemies will have a corresponding gear  or difficulty level like they did in far  cry new dawn where players needed to  keep up with their weapon levels to do  proper damage  in that game players didn't have to  worry about their clothing and armor  though we did ask about how much of new  dawn systems would come over to far cry  6 in an interview but we didn't get a  specific answer  although not referred to in this  presentation as fangs for hire  there are pets in this game including  guapo the alligator that can chomp your  enemies  and chorizo who is very cute and  distracting to let you commit  silent murders  so that's guns and gear let's talk about  transportation inspired by the isolation  of cuba the island of yara is stuck in  time which means modern technology is  kind of rare  many of the guns and vehicles you'll  find are repurposed from old stuff  there's a wide range of transportation  like horses and aging cars but from  there players can build up mad max style  technicals with all kinds of weapons and  attachments bolted on  you can also hijack a tank regarding  flying things  the game seems like it's going to  attempt to keep you grounded for a while  with flat cannons scattered around the  island  this is kind of nice as much as we like  flying helicopters it's always kind of  broken far cry games by letting you go  from objective to objective without  really engaging in the world  it's possible you'll be able to blow  these up quickly and do it anyway but  we're hoping flying's more of a late  game thing  alright so who are you you play as danny  rojas who can be either male or female  unlike most other far cry games dany is  fully voiced and will appear in  cutscenes  they live on the island of yara which is  being ravaged by a brutal dictator named  anton castillo  played by actor gene carlo esposito the  island's been isolated for about 50  years leading to some urban decay  his goal is to return yard to its former  glory with the help of  about 300 000 soldiers and a bit of  martial law his son diego seems like an  unwilling participant but we'll have to  see how that pans out  if you remember you played the role of a  son in a similar situation in far cry 4  and wound up potentially being just as  bad as your old pops  dany is a military dropout and their  family was part of the regime previously  so their story might be echoed in diego  to fight the good fight you're working  with a local revolutionary leader clara  garcia and her army of guerilla rebels  so what does that mean from a gameplay  perspective you'll find a lot of the  usual activities like taking checkpoints  and outposts plus stomping around the  jungle on trails in search of hidden  loot but you'll also be in the  huge capital city with its skyscrapers  in underground areas and that kind of  urban scale is new to the series  on a side note we also saw some mini  games like playing dominoes  seems like a nice way to unwind overall  the presentation didn't answer all of  our questions like if far cry 6 will  continue the more heavy-handed rpg  systems of new dawn which were a bit  divisive with fans  we can't wait to get our hands on the  game and really put that weapon  customization to the test  despite the heavy political setting that  centers around a malevolent dictator far  cry 6 does not seem to be taking its  moment to moment gameplay too seriously  there will be more to say about this  game soon as e3 kicks off this june  so be sure to subscribe to gamespot's  youtube page and we'll keep you up to  date  thanks for watching  [Music]  do  [Music]  you
 

